/* F's parameter ranges over the trees qe accepts, and input trees may be
   infinite: qe accepts e(e(e(...))), although no finite tree (its only
   transition needs another e below).  So there is an input, and F ignores
   it and returns bad, which qo rejects.  A reading of the input automaton
   over finite trees only finds no input and answers sat vacuously. */
%BEGING
F x -> bad.
%ENDG

%BEGINA
qe e -> qe.
qo ok -> .
%ENDA

%BEGINT
F : qe -> qo.
%ENDT
